node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
# Windows alternate-data-stream artefacts
*:Zone.Identifier
*:mshield
# Corpus harness downloads: public documents, but large and re-fetchable.
.corpus-cache/
corpus-report.json
answer-key-report.json
# The retrieved-document cache, if IBID_CACHE_DIR is ever pointed inside the tree. It
# defaults to a platform cache directory outside any checkout — this is a guard, not the
# usual location. See docs/DATA-FLOW.md.
.ibid-cache/


# The sample folder is an allow-list, not a deny-list. The constructed documents are named
# here and everything else in it is local to the machine that put it there.
#
# That direction is the point. This is the folder a real document gets dropped into while
# something is being checked against it, and a deny-list only ever excludes the files someone
# thought to name. Whatever is tested here next is unpublished by default, and adding a
# constructed sample is one deliberate line.
samples/ibid-demo-docx/*
!samples/ibid-demo-docx/README.md
!samples/ibid-demo-docx/*.py
!samples/ibid-demo-docx/EU_Data_Retention_Memo.docx
!samples/ibid-demo-docx/eu-case-law-citation-test.docx
!samples/ibid-demo-docx/back-reference-test.docx

# Word lock files, written beside a document while it is open.
~$*

# Throwaway trial state: the tunnel URL of the day, its logs, and the add-in Id.
# The Id is deliberately kept across runs but is local to this machine.
.trial/

# Accuracy sampling: marking sheets carry the text of real footnotes, so a sheet is as
# confidential as the document it was drawn from. The scripts that produce them are in the
# repository; their output never is. See docs/ACCURACY.md.
.accuracy/
